            <ArticleTitle>Asymmetric synthesis of 4-aryl-1,2,5-thiadiazolidin-3-one 1,1-dioxides via Pd-catalyzed hydrogenation of cyclic ketimines.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1325-1328</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1039/c6ob02655a</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>An efficient access to optically active sulfahydantoins, 4-aryl-1,2,5-thiadiazolidin-3-one 1,1-dioxides, was developed through palladium-catalyzed asymmetric hydrogenation of the corresponding cyclic N-sulfonylketimines with up to 98% ee.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
